## Decisions and Next Steps

* **No Adoption Decision:** The working group did not reach consensus on whether a sufficiently defined problem exists to justify adopting the draft. 
* **Next Steps:** Dick Hardt indicated he will consider whether to continue pursuing this work within OAUTH. To build a compelling case for future adoption, the draft would need to be updated in collaboration with security researchers (such as Jonas) to explicitly map out the exact attack models and surfaces (such as the Browser-Swapping Attack) that the proposed header-based flow successfully mitigates. Dick Hardt also noted that alternative protocols like GNAP inherently resolve these redirect-loop security issues.